WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.260
Every film starts with an idea and

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.680
a blank timeline.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.600
Meet AuteurFrame, an open-source motion studio powered

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.440
by a team of AI agents.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:11.740
Type a brief,

6
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.300
and the swarm gets to work.

7
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.620
A research scout pulls real facts from

8
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.040
the web.

9
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.340
A director writes the screenplay and sets

10
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:18.760
the look.

11
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.300
A narrator voices it,

12
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.280
and a crew of animators builds every

13
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.260
scene from scratch,

14
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.780
all at the same time.

15
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.280
Then a critic watches every shot and

16
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.920
sends it back until it's right.

17
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.280
A sound designer adds music and effects,

18
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.240
and the editor masters it in full

19
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.040
HD with captions in sync.

20
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.940
And you're always in control.

21
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.340
Drag, trim, and split on a real

22
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.760
timeline, or right-click and ask an agent

23
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.260
to rebuild a single shot.

24
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.040
Photos, footage, maps,

25
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.500
and voices come free with no API

26
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.540
keys, and it works with any model

27
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:49.960
you like.

28
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.740
Today, AuteurFrame is open source.

29
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:53.520
This film?

30
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.200
Made with AuteurFrame.

31
00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.080
Now, what will you make?
